                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Pros:\r\n+ Humor\r\n+ Great vibes to the entire series\r\n+ Has good length and do not drag things out\r\n+ Despite it's age, still plays great\r\n\r\nCons:\r\n- Sword fighting can get tedious\r\n- Puzzles do not use logic, but humor and are chaotic\r\n\r\nLegendary game and must play for all adventure game fans. Humor is great and the game has aged surprisingly well. But it has the same problem all Monkey Island(tm) games have - you cannot solve any of the puzzles by thinking logically, because nothing is logical in Monkey Island(tm). You have to put yourself into shoes of Ron Gilbert and Tim Schafer and think how they would think to solve anything. Think what they would think is funny rather than what makes logical sense. There's little backtracking here and there, but overall first game is pretty straight forward and not that long. And it is still fun.",
